The Open Cybersecurity Schema Framework
---------------------------------------

src/ocsf/schema/, src/ocsf/datamodel/ and project/ render the Open Cybersecurity
Schema Framework, version 1.9.0, which the OCSF project publishes at
https://github.com/ocsf/ocsf-schema under the Apache License, Version 2.0. Its
captions and descriptions are copied into the schema from there, and this project's
own text is the rest. This project is not the OCSF project's, and OCSF's marks are
its own. The framework's NOTICE reads:

  Open Cybersecurity Schema Framework

  Copyright © OCSF a Series of LF Projects, LLC
  For web site terms of use, trademark policy and other project policies please
  see https://lfprojects.org.

  This project includes the ICD Schema developed by Symantec, a division of
  Broadcom.

  Licensed under the Apache 2 license.
  Refer to the Apache 2 license in the file LICENSE.

upstream/ocsf-schema/ holds the tag's files unchanged, with its LICENSE and NOTICE,
and scripts/check_upstream_release.py pins each by its git object hash.
upstream/ocsf-compiled-1.9.0.json is the output of ocsf-schema-compiler 1.1.1, the OCSF
project's own tool under the same licence, over that folder, unchanged.

tests/data/ocsf-server-samples-1.9.0.json.gz holds what https://schema.ocsf.io/sample/
answered for each event class on 2026-11-04. That server is ocsf-server, under the
same licence, and each answer is random words in the framework's shape.

ocsf/examples, the OCSF project's repository of sample events, states no licence, so
no event of it is copied here. scripts/check_real_events.py reads them at a pinned
commit and tests/upstream/ocsf-examples-verdicts.json holds only their paths, their
git object hashes and what OCSF's validator found.

